#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:153
msgid "Filesystem write outside the writable paths"
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:159
msgid "A write, delete, move or permission-change call whose target does not resolve to the uploads directory or /tmp/."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:160
msgid "Application code on WordPress VIP is deployed from Git onto a read-only filesystem. Only /tmp/ and /wp-content/uploads/ accept writes. Writing anywhere else — including into a plugin or theme directory — fails at runtime."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:161
msgid "Point the write at the uploads directory using wp_get_upload_dir(), or at get_temp_dir() for scratch data that does not need to survive the request. Never build the path by concatenating WP_CONTENT_DIR, plugin_dir_path() or __DIR__."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:162
msgid "If the data is state rather than a file, store it in an option, post meta, a custom table or the object cache instead of on disk."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:192
msgid "File opened for writing outside the writable paths"
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:198
msgid "fopen() called with a write, append or truncate mode on a path that does not resolve to uploads or /tmp/."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:199
msgid "Opening a file for reading is fine on WordPress VIP. Opening one for writing outside /tmp/ and the uploads directory fails, because the application filesystem is read-only."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:200
msgid "Write to a path built from wp_get_upload_dir(), or to get_temp_dir() for transient scratch files. The WordPress VIP stream wrapper makes fopen(), fwrite() and fclose() work normally inside /wp-content/uploads/."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:201
msgid "For read-only access to a bundled data file, keep the current path and the \"r\" mode — that is supported."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:210
msgid "Hard-coded uploads path"
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:216
msgid "A literal \"wp-content/uploads\" path in the source."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:217
msgid "On WordPress VIP the uploads directory is mapped onto an external object store, and on multisite each subsite writes under its own prefix. A hard-coded path resolves to the wrong location, or to nothing at all."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:218
msgid "Replace the literal with wp_get_upload_dir() (paths) or wp_upload_dir()[\"baseurl\"] (URLs) and append the sub-path to the returned value."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:219
msgid "For a static asset that ships with the code, reference it with plugins_url() or get_theme_file_uri() instead of putting it in uploads."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:229
msgid "Legacy blogs.dir media path"
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:235
msgid "A reference to the pre-3.5 multisite blogs.dir media directory."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:236
msgid "WordPress VIP only serves and accepts media under /wp-content/uploads/. Media stored in wp-content/blogs.dir is neither importable nor reachable, so anything that reads or writes there breaks."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:237
msgid "Move the media into the uploads directory, update the stored paths in the database with a targeted search-and-replace, and add redirects for the old URLs."
msgstr ""

