msgid "Directory iteration over uploads"
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:254
msgid "A directory listing or traversal call pointed at the uploads directory."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:255
msgid "The WordPress VIP File System is an object store presented through a stream wrapper, with no real directory tree. On the uploads directory, scandir(), glob(), opendir() and similar calls return an empty array or false and raise a PHP warning. Directory traversal only works in /tmp."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:256
msgid "Stop discovering files by listing a directory. Record the files you write — in post meta, user meta, an option or a custom table — and read that index back instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:257
msgid "For attachments, query the media library with WP_Query on the \"attachment\" post type rather than walking the uploads folder."
msgstr ""

