#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:273
msgid "Code that reads, writes or depends on .htaccess or the Apache API."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:274
msgid "WordPress VIP serves requests through NGINX. There is no .htaccess file, the Apache functions do not exist, and the web root is not writable, so rewrite rules, deny rules and header rules written this way are silently ignored."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:275
msgid "Express redirects in PHP — wp_safe_redirect() on the \"template_redirect\" hook, or the Safe Redirect Manager plugin. Domain-level redirects belong in vip-config.php. Access rules belong in application code."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:276
msgid "Send headers with the WordPress HTTP API and the \"wp_headers\" filter rather than through server configuration."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:287
msgid "Dynamically generated PHP, CSS or JS file"
