#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:293
msgid "A write whose target filename ends in .php, .css, .js, .html or .json."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:294
msgid "Generating code or asset files at runtime assumes a writable application directory, which WordPress VIP does not provide. Even when the write lands in uploads, generated PHP is never executed there, and generated CSS or JS bypasses the platform asset pipeline."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:295
msgid "Build the asset at deploy time and commit it, or render it through a WordPress endpoint (wp_add_inline_style(), wp_add_inline_script(), or a registered REST route) instead of writing a file."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:296
msgid "For configuration that used to be written to a PHP file, store it in an option and read it back through get_option()."
msgstr ""

