msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:329
msgid "Media on WordPress VIP can only be written to paths beginning /wp-content/uploads/. A filter that redirects uploads elsewhere — a plugin folder, a sibling directory, a third-party bucket — produces failed uploads or missing thumbnails."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:330
msgid "Keep the base directory as WordPress VIP supplies it and only vary the sub-path underneath it. Confirm the filter still returns a path inside the uploads base directory."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:331
msgid "Organise media with taxonomy or post meta instead of custom folder layouts."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:339
msgid "Local image processing"
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:345
msgid "Direct use of GD or Imagick to resize, crop or re-encode images."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:346
msgid "WordPress VIP resizes, crops and re-encodes images on the fly at the CDN edge from the original upload. Doing the same work in PHP spends request time on something the platform already provides, and writes extra derivative files into the file system."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:347
msgid "Request the size you need through the image URL and let the platform generate it, or use wp_get_attachment_image() with a registered size."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:348
msgid "Where bespoke processing is genuinely required, run it once on upload rather than on every page render."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:369
msgid "Registered intermediate image sizes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:375
msgid "A call to add_image_size()."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:376
msgid "WordPress VIP does not create a file for each registered size. Every size is generated on request from the original through URL parameters, and get_intermediate_image_sizes() returns an empty array. Code that expects a resized file on disk, or loops over the size list, will not find what it expects."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:377
msgid "Keep registered sizes for wp_get_attachment_image() and srcset, but never read a resized file from disk. Request one-off dimensions with URL parameters such as ?w=300&h=200&crop=1."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:397
msgid "SQL built by interpolation instead of $wpdb->prepare()"
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:403
msgid "A $wpdb query whose SQL contains an interpolated or concatenated variable, with no $wpdb->prepare() call."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:404
msgid "This is a SQL injection vector. WordPress VIP code review blocks unprepared queries, and the WordPress VIP Code Analysis Bot reports them on every pull request."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:408
msgid "Wrap the SQL in $wpdb->prepare() using its string, integer and float placeholders, and pass the values as arguments. Table names cannot be placeholders — build them from $wpdb->prefix and validate against a known list."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:409
msgid "Prefer a core API — WP_Query, get_posts(), get_terms() — over hand-written SQL wherever one exists."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:419
msgid "Direct database query"
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:425
msgid "A $wpdb query that bypasses the WordPress data APIs."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:426
msgid "WordPress VIP runs behind HyperDB, which splits reads across replicas. Hand-written queries skip the object cache entirely, so each one is a round trip on every request, and they are the usual cause of slow pages at traffic."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:427
msgid "Use a core API where one exists. Where a direct query is genuinely needed, wrap the result in wp_cache_get()/wp_cache_set() with an explicit group and expiry."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:428
msgid "For search and heavy filtering, use WordPress VIP Search (Enterprise Search) rather than SQL."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:438
msgid "Runtime database schema change"
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:444
msgid "CREATE TABLE, ALTER TABLE, DROP TABLE, TRUNCATE TABLE or dbDelta() in application code."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:445
msgid "Custom tables are allowed on WordPress VIP, but they must use the $wpdb->prefix table prefix, and a schema change issued on every web request can lock tables on a production database."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:446
msgid "Run schema changes through dbDelta() from a versioned upgrade routine that runs once, such as an option-version check or a WP-CLI command, never on every request. Use the $wpdb->prefix prefix and a WordPress VIP-supported utf8mb4 collation."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:447
msgid "Consider whether a custom post type, taxonomy or meta table can replace the custom table before adding one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:460
msgid "Uncached lookup function"
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:466
msgid "A core function that WordPress VIP documents as running an uncached database query."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:467
msgid "These functions query the database directly on every call with no object-cache layer in front of them. On a high-traffic site they turn into an uncached query per page view."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:468
msgid "Use the cached wrapper WordPress VIP provides: wpcom_vip_url_to_postid(), wpcom_vip_attachment_url_to_postid(), wpcom_vip_count_user_posts(), wpcom_vip_get_adjacent_post(), wpcom_vip_wp_oembed_get() or wpcom_vip_old_slug_redirect(). Otherwise cache the result yourself with wp_cache_get() and wp_cache_set()."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:469
msgid "Store the resolved ID alongside the data that needed it so the lookup only happens once."
