#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:509
msgid "Query argument known to be expensive"
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:515
msgid "A query using post__not_in, an unindexed meta_query, or orderby => rand."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:516
msgid "These arguments generate SQL the database cannot serve from an index. Random ordering also defeats caching entirely, because every response differs."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:517
msgid "Replace post__not_in by over-fetching slightly and filtering in PHP. Replace random ordering by selecting a random slice from a cached ID list. Where meta filtering drives the query, move it to WordPress VIP Search."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:518
msgid "Model the filter as a taxonomy term instead of post meta — taxonomy queries are indexed."
