msgid "Scope the header to genuinely per-user responses. Where the page is mostly static with a small dynamic part, cache the page and load the dynamic fragment separately."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:717
msgid "Send a Cache-Control header with a shorter max-age instead of disabling caching outright."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:726
msgid "Cookie set on a front-end response"
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:732
msgid "A call to setcookie() or setrawcookie()."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:733
msgid "A response that sends a Set-Cookie header through setcookie() is marked uncacheable by the WordPress VIP page cache. Set on every front-end page, it takes the site off the edge cache."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:734
msgid "Set the cookie only on the responses that genuinely need it, or in JavaScript after the cached page loads, so the HTML itself stays cacheable."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:735
msgid "To serve different cached versions to groups of visitors, use the WordPress VIP cache personalization API (the Vary_Cache class) instead of a custom cookie."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:754
msgid "WP-Cron constant defined in application code"
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:760
msgid "DISABLE_WP_CRON, ALTERNATE_WP_CRON or WP_CRON_LOCK_TIMEOUT defined by a plugin or theme."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:761
msgid "WordPress VIP replaces WP-Cron with Cron Control, which runs events from a managed runner rather than from page loads. Redefining these constants either does nothing or interferes with the platform runner."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:762
msgid "Remove the constant. Cron Control already guarantees that scheduled events run without depending on site traffic."
msgstr ""

