#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:797
msgid "A callback registered on the cron_schedules filter."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:798
msgid "By default Cron Control runs only one event with the same action at a time. If the interval is shorter than the job takes, runs queue up rather than happening more often."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:799
msgid "Check that the job finishes well inside the interval, and split long jobs into batches. Schedule recurring work with wp_schedule_event(), not by calling wp_schedule_single_event() again on every run."
