msgid "A superglobal printed directly by echo or print."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:881
msgid "This is a reflected cross-site scripting vector. WordPress VIP code review treats unescaped output as a blocker."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:882
msgid "Sanitise on input with sanitize_text_field( wp_unslash( ... ) ) and escape on output with esc_html(), esc_attr() or esc_url() as appropriate."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:892
msgid "extract() imports variables from an array"
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:898
msgid "A call to extract()."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:899
msgid "extract() creates variables whose names come from data, so it can overwrite existing variables and makes the surrounding code impossible to reason about or review."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:900
msgid "Read the array keys explicitly, or destructure with list()/[] so the variable names are visible in the source."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:910
msgid "File included from a variable path"
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:916
msgid "include or require whose path is built from a variable."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:917
msgid "If any part of the path can be influenced by input, this is a local file inclusion vulnerability."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:918
msgid "Validate the variable against an explicit allow-list of filenames before including it, and anchor the path to a known base directory."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:919
msgid "For template loading, use locate_template() or get_template_part(), which resolve against the theme only."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:928
msgid "PHP file with no direct-access guard"
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:934
msgid "A PHP file that declares functions or classes without checking for ABSPATH first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:935
msgid "Without the guard the file executes if it is requested directly, outside the WordPress bootstrap, which can expose errors or run code without any of the usual context."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:936
msgid "Add defined( 'ABSPATH' ) || exit; near the top of the file, below the file docblock."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:956
msgid "PHP session used"
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:962
msgid "session_start(), another session function, or $_SESSION."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:963
msgid "WordPress VIP supports PHP sessions for short-lived data, backed by Memcached, but every request from a user with a session bypasses the page cache. Starting a session for every visitor takes the site off the edge cache."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:964
msgid "Start a session only when it is needed, scope it with the path argument of session_set_cookie_params(), and destroy it as soon as the flow is done."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:965
msgid "For logged-in users, user meta is often a better home for per-user state, and it is already cached."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:975
msgid "PHP runtime setting changed at request time"
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:981
msgid "ini_set(), set_time_limit(), error_reporting(), putenv(), dl() or date_default_timezone_set()."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:982
msgid "PHP configuration on WordPress VIP is managed by the platform. These calls are either ignored or overridden, so code that depends on the new value behaves differently in production than it does locally."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:983
msgid "Remove the call and make the code work within the platform limits. If a limit genuinely blocks the workload, raise it with WordPress VIP support rather than trying to change it from PHP."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:984
msgid "Work that needs a long execution time belongs in a WP-CLI command or a batched cron job, not a web request."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:993
msgid "Assumption about the server or filesystem layout"
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:999
