msgid "mail() used instead of wp_mail()"
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:1070
msgid "A call to PHP's mail() function."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:1071
msgid "WordPress VIP code review flags application code that generates email, and expects any mail that must be sent to go through wp_mail(). PHP mail() bypasses the hooks WordPress and its plugins use to deliver, filter and log mail."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:1072
msgid "Replace mail() with wp_mail(). The arguments map directly."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:1082
msgid "switch_to_blog() without a matching restore"
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:1088
msgid "switch_to_blog() with no restore_current_blog() in the same function."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:1089
msgid "Leaving the site switched corrupts every subsequent query and cache read in the request, and the bug surfaces far from its cause. Switching is also expensive, so doing it inside a loop is a common source of slow pages on multisite."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:1090
msgid "Pair every switch_to_blog() with restore_current_blog(), including on early-return and exception paths."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:1091
msgid "Where the data is read repeatedly across sites, collect it once and cache it rather than switching per item."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:1109
msgid "flush_rewrite_rules() called at runtime"
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:1115
msgid "A call to flush_rewrite_rules()."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:1116
msgid "Regenerating the rewrite rules is expensive and writes a large autoloaded option. Called on a hook such as \"init\" it runs on every request, which WordPress VIP treats as a serious performance defect."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:1117
msgid "Call it only from an activation hook or a WP-CLI command, never on a request-time hook."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:1127
msgid "wp_redirect() instead of wp_safe_redirect()"
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:1133
msgid "A call to wp_redirect()."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:1134
msgid "wp_redirect() will send a visitor to any host. When the destination comes from a request parameter that is an open-redirect vulnerability."
msgstr ""

#: includes/scanner/class-rules.php:1135
msgid "Use wp_safe_redirect(), which restricts the destination to allowed hosts, and add external hosts with the \"allowed_redirect_hosts\" filter when you need them."
msgstr ""

